      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.caesura" resname="help.caesura">
        <source>The grading scale turns a percentage of the maximum score into a grade. Between two points the grade changes evenly. Below the first point the grade stays at the first grade, and at the top it stops at the last grade.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.caesura_pass" resname="help.caesura_pass">
        <source>Passing is decided on the exact percentage, not on the rounded grade. A student can therefore see a 5.5 and still have failed, if the score was just under the pass mark.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.flags_title" resname="help.flags_title">
        <source>Why a question is marked</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.flags" resname="help.flags">
        <source>By default a question is marked when its difficulty is below 0.30 or above 0.90, or when its discrimination is below 0.20. A negative discrimination is always marked, because that often means the answer key is wrong. You can change the boundaries under Adjust analysis.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.adjust_title" resname="help.adjust_title">
        <source>Trying a change</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.adjust" resname="help.adjust">
        <source>Leaving a question out removes its points from the maximum and from every student, and the grades are calculated again.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.adjust_full" resname="help.adjust_full">
        <source>Giving everyone full marks keeps the question's points but assumes every student got them, for example after a wrong answer key.</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.privacy_title" resname="help.privacy_title">
        <source>Your students' results</source>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.privacy" resname="help.privacy">
        <source>The file is read into memory for the analysis and is not saved. When you adjust the analysis, the same data is sent again with the page. Close the page and it is gone.</source>
      </trans-unit>
